sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor U as user
  participant B as tui.updateBoard
  participant P as tui.updateSessions (modeSessions)
  participant V as tui.viewSessions
  participant F as huh form (newForm)
  participant C as tui.reassign (one producer)
  participant L as launch (tmux)
  participant R as readers (dot, cap, lock, sweep)

  U->>B: S
  B->>P: mode = modeSessions, sessIdx = 0
  P->>V: render rows from cached m.sessionMeta
  V-->>U: name · bound item / unbound · repo · age · attached
  V-->>U: empty panel names its reason - no live gogo-* sessions / tmux not installed

  Note over P,V: the 5s sessionTick keeps m.sessionMeta fresh in every mode
  Note over P,V: the cursor clamps when the list shrinks

  U->>P: R - re-assign the highlighted session
  P->>F: Select of DRIVABLE work items - slug · status · resulting name - plus Cancel
  U->>F: pick a work item
  F->>C: finishReassignSession(session, target)
  C->>C: refusals - already bound, foreign session_path anchor
  alt refused
    C-->>U: status line names the reason and the unblock (amber)
  else accepted
    C->>L: renamer to RenameSessionUnique(old, SessionNameFor(bindAction(target), slug))
    L-->>C: final name, with a -2 / -3 collision suffix if taken
    C->>P: refreshSessions and stay in modeSessions
    C-->>U: re-assigned old to new (ok)
    L-->>R: next tick re-derives every binding from the NAME
  end

  U->>P: K - close the highlighted session
  P->>F: destructive confirm, Cancel default, names the exact session
  U->>F: Kill
  F->>L: killer to KillSession(name) - kill-session -t =name
  L-->>P: refreshSessions, cursor clamps, stay in the panel
  alt tmux failed
    P-->>U: failure carrying tmux own words (red)
  else killed
    P-->>U: killed 1 session (ok)
  end

  U->>P: esc / q
  P->>B: mode = modeBoard

  Note over C,R: no pipeline state is written anywhere here
  Note over C,R: renaming and killing a tmux session are not state writes
